# Slow Cooker Chicken Tortilla Soup

Based on a recipe shared by Becky Harder from Monument, CO

{ rating="5" image="slow_cooker_chicken_tortilla_soup.jpg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Toppings

- [ ] [Tortilla chips]{ ing="tortilla-chips" }
- [ ] 2 cups [grated cheese]{ ing="grated-cheese" }
- [ ] [Sour cream]{ ing="sour-cream" }

### Soup

- [ ] 2 large [chicken breast]{ ing="chicken-breast" }, halved
- [ ] 2 cans of [black beans]{ ing="black-beans" } (30 oz)
- [ ] 3 cans of Original Rotel [Diced Tomatoes and Green Chilies]{ ing="diced-tomatoes-and-green-chilies" } (30 oz)

      - Or 3-4 large tomatoes, diced
- [ ] 1 cup [salsa]{ ing="salsa" }
- [ ] 4 oz [green chilies]{ ing="green-chilies" }, chopped
- [ ] 14.5 oz can [tomato sauce]{ ing="tomato-sauce" }

## Recipe

1. Halve the [chicken breasts]{ ing="chicken-breast" }, then combine all the ingredients (undrained) into a crock pot (*makes exactly 3 Qt). Cover and cook on low for 8 hours
1. Just before serving, slice the [chicken breasts]{ ing="chicken-breast" } into bite size pieces and return to soup
